Let $J$ be Jerry's current age.
Five years ago, Jerry's age was $J-5$.
According to the problem, Jerry is twice as old as he was 5 years ago.
So, $J = 2(J-5)$.
$J = 2J - 10$
$J - 2J = -10$
$-J = -10$
$J = 10$
Jerry's current age is 10 years old.
In 3 years, Jerry's age will be $J + 3 = 10 + 3 = 13$.

